    "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-136015: the first binomial coefficients are 1, 8, 28, with alternating signs. q-136012: the first terms are (2x)^5, -5(2x)^4y, and 10(2x)^3y^2. q-18624: the coefficient is binom(15,12)·2^3=3640. q-113621: x^18 requires six x^3 factors, giving binom(10,6)·2^4=3360. q-77789: the solutions are π/6 and 5π/6, whose product is 5π²/36. q-77812: the equations require cosecant values 10, 1/3, and 4; only II violates |csc x|≥1. q-70958: row 2 dotted with column 5 gives 3·10−4·7=2. q-13635: the outer product has rows (0,0), (−2,−4), (−3,−6). q-1045: transposition converts the row into a column without changing entry order. q-76493: the angles are approximately 106.601549° and 253.398451°; their product is approximately 27012.667, rounding to 27013. q-120485: the required secant values are 7, 2/√3, and −5/7; only III violates |sec x|≥1. q-46588: 3(y−3)^2=3y²−18y+27. q-46669: 2((v−3)^2+16)=2v²−12v+50. q-77717: T(x,y)=(2x−y,4x+y), giving A′=(5,7), B′=(−9,−3). q-159801: T(x,y)=(x+2y,2x), giving A′=(6,4), B′=(1,−6), C′=(−3,2). q-8093: T(x,y)=(x−y,x+y), giving A′=(−1,3), B′=(0,6), C′=(0,8), D′=(−1,5). Source errors do occur in exposition: the binomial solutions print fractions where binomial coefficients are intended; q-70958 incorrectly equates the scalar r25 with the entire matrix product in its first line; q-159801 and q-8093 incorrectly say 'image of T under the action of T.' These errors do not alter the stated answers. No submitted grade or earlier solver answer was supplied; confirmation uses the captured worked solutions.",
